-- Configure the blends that can be applied to each overlay layer. Feel free to add new ones or modify.
-- Don't forget to also update "client/creator/config.lua" with the new blends for them to be available.
-- Multiple cut or unused albedos and sheetIndeces are already included in the configuration by default.

-- Blend data structure reference:
-- albedo:         (string) Base color map or texture index
-- normal:         (string) Surface depth/bump map for 3D detail, unused by default
-- material:       (string) Physical material type or surface identifier, unused by default
-- texAlpha:       (number) Primary texture opacity level Acts as the 100% value for the creator slider
-- blendType:      (number) Mathematical mode for mixing textures (0, 1, 2)
-- roughness:      (number) Surface finish: higher is matte, lower is glossy
-- sheetGridIndex: (number) Cell index within a texture atlas grid
-- modTexture:     (string) Secondary texture used for masking or modification
-- modChannel:     (number) Selection of source channel (R, G, B) for modification
-- modAlpha:       (number) Intensity or opacity of the modification effect
-- palette:        (string) Color palette ID selection (METAPED_TINT_GENERIC, METAPED_TINT_GENERIC_CLEAN, METAPED_TINT_GENERIC_WEATHERED, METAPED_TINT_HAIR, etc)
-- tint:           (number) Shorthand to apply a single value to all three tint channels
-- tint0:          (number) Color tint for channel 0 (typically the R channel)
-- tint1:          (number) Color tint for channel 1 (typically the G channel)
-- tint2:          (number) Color tint for channel 2 (typically the B channel)

-- Some blends are hair color specific. In this case, make sure to match CreatorConfig.HairColors.
-- This applies to EYEBROWS, FACIAL_HAIR and HEAD_HAIR blends. If a color is missing, you'll get an error.

